Refine the existing QuickBite Operations Dashboard to make it cleaner, simpler, and easier to explain during a Senior AI Data Operations Manager case-study presentation.

IMPORTANT:
- Do NOT rebuild the application.
- Do NOT change the existing approved order schema, calculations, synthetic datasets, routing, upload functionality, or working business logic.
- Preserve all existing functionality unless explicitly requested below.
- Focus primarily on information architecture, removing duplication, simplifying terminology, and improving visual hierarchy.
- Keep the existing professional visual style.

The dashboard should tell one simple end-to-end story:

Overview → Is the system healthy?
Data → Can I trust the data?
Metrics → Where is the model failing?
Issues → What should Data Ops do about it?

-----------------------------------
1. OVERVIEW PAGE
-----------------------------------

Simplify the Overview into four compact sections:

A. Model Health
Show only the most important model KPIs:
- MAE
- P90 Error
- Within ±10 min
- Underprediction Rate

B. Operational Health
Show compact KPIs for:
- Data Readiness
- Open P0 Issues
- Active Vendor Batches
- Annotation QA

C. Needs Attention
Show only the top 3 highest-priority issues, for example:
- Mumbai × Heavy Rain
- Bengaluru × Rider Reassignment
- New Restaurants

Each should show severity, cohort, key performance degradation, and a link/action to view the issue.

D. Vendor & Batch Status
Keep the existing Batch Intake / Vendor Batch functionality, but make it compact.
Display:
- Batch ID
- Vendor
- Progress %
- QA Score
- SLA
- Status

Support multiple vendors such as Vendor-A, Vendor-B, and Internal QA.

REMOVE or heavily simplify the existing “Operating Posture / Signal Board” because it duplicates information available elsewhere.

-----------------------------------
2. DATA PAGE
-----------------------------------

Keep the existing governed ingestion workflow:
Upload → Schema Validation → Data Quality → Preview → Classification → Approve Ingestion.

Keep:
- Data Readiness
- Annotation QA
- Human approval
- Existing validation logic

Rename “Manual Edge-Case Entry” to:

“Proactive Edge Case Intake”

Add a short description:
“Log known upcoming operational risks before they appear as production model failures.”

This should remain separate from automated issue detection and can capture risks such as:
- new city launches
- upcoming festivals
- severe weather
- operational changes
- new restaurant cohorts

Do not change the approved order schema.

-----------------------------------
3. METRICS PAGE
-----------------------------------

Keep this page analytical and focused only on:

Global Performance
→ Service Surface by City
→ Cohort Drill-Down

Keep:
- MAE
- P90
- Within ±10 min
- Underprediction
- City comparison
- Existing filters/drill-downs

Do NOT add vendor, annotation, edge-case intake, or operational workflow information here.

The purpose of this page is simply:
“Where is the model failing?”

-----------------------------------
4. ISSUES PAGE
-----------------------------------

Merge “Emerging Issues & Action Queue” and “Edge Case Radar” into one unified section:

“Issues & Edge Cases”

Do not show the same incident twice.

Each issue should clearly present:

Signal
→ Evidence
→ Root-Cause Hypothesis
→ Recommended Data Action
→ Human Decision

Show:
- P0/P1/P2
- Cohort
- MAE
- Baseline MAE
- P90 where available
- Underprediction
- Affected records/sample size
- Performance degradation
- Suspected cause
- Recommended Data Ops action
- Human approval/review status

Keep Targeted Data Acquisition as a major part of this page.

For a selected issue show a compact Targeted Data Plan with:
- Cohort
- Data role: Baseline / Seasonal / Edge Case
- Current coverage
- Desired coverage
- Coverage gap
- Sampling strategy
- Annotation priority
- Reason for collection

The purpose should be:
“Do not collect more data. Collect the data required to close a demonstrated model gap.”

-----------------------------------
5. TERMINOLOGY CLEANUP
-----------------------------------

Reduce terminology overload throughout the UI.

Prefer these simple labels:

- Model Health
- Data Health
- Vendor Batches
- City Performance
- Issues & Edge Cases
- Targeted Data Plan
- Proactive Edge Case Intake

Avoid introducing additional names for the same concepts.

-----------------------------------
6. FINAL USER EXPERIENCE
-----------------------------------

The finished application should make this workflow immediately understandable:

Production
→ Monitor
→ Detect
→ Triage
→ Target Data
→ Vendor / Human Review
→ QA
→ Evaluate
→ Retrain
→ Regression Test
→ Human Approval
→ Production

The application should feel like an AI Data Operations decision-support system, not a collection of unrelated dashboards.

AI can detect, triage, and recommend, but humans should remain responsible for consequential actions.

Keep the interface compact and presentation-friendly. Avoid adding new cards or sections unless they directly support the four core questions.

Before finishing, verify that all existing routes, data upload, calculations, filters, issue detection, human decisions, and vendor batch functionality still work.
